 "summary": "s24vmm reserves the SCFB region directly below the FDT and streams S24F frames from the seqlocked SCFB (frame_seq, POLL, DAMAGE, drawing/host_reading) to one localhost viewer. Its virtio-mmio v2 virtio-input multitouch device at 0x0a000000 (SPI 16 = INTID 48) reports MT-B events through KVM_IRQ_LINE. Host tests pass: test_vmm 220 checks, test_io 92 under ASan+UBSan, the seqlock test under TSan, and a warning-free static NDK build. The SCFB header offsets match both pinned scion-avf structs. The viewer APK decodes the VMM C encoder output on the host JVM, 39 checks, and the C decoder reads its touches back. Two clean builds in each of two runs gave the same unsigned aligned APK. Nothing was run on the device.",
